+# Kanhu Murmu's Role in the Santhal Hul Uprising
+
+Kanhu Murmu was a prominent leader of the Santhal Hul uprising against British colonial rule in 1855-1860. Born into a poor family in Santhal Pargana, he played a crucial role in organizing and leading the movement.
+
+## Historical Context
+The Santhal Hul, also known as the Santhal Rebellion or the Kantha Rebellion, was one of the earliest anti-colonial uprisings in India. It began when the British introduced a new tax on salt in 1854, which deeply affected the Santhals.
+
+## Murmu's Involvement
+Kanhu Murmu and his followers attacked several British settlements in the region, causing significant damage. His military strategies, including guerrilla warfare tactics, were effective against the colonial forces.
+
+## Impact on the Movement
+Murmu's leadership was pivotal in maintaining the spirit of resistance among the Santhals. His actions inspired many others to join the uprising, leading to a widespread rebellion that eventually forced the British to negotiate.
+
+## Legacy
+Kanhu Murmu is remembered as a hero for his courage and selflessness in fighting against colonial oppression. Today, he continues to be celebrated as a symbol of resistance and national pride.
